composer require laravel/breeze --dev
What does --dev mean?
It installs Breeze as a development dependency used to generate the application's authentication scaffolding. The generated application code remains in your project.

php artisan breeze:install blade

npm install

Breeze uses Vite and frontend dependencies to build its CSS and JavaScript.

npm run build

Then build the frontend assets:

php artisan migrate

Run Laravel migrations

composer run dev start the application

In a fresh Laravel 12 project, the dev script in composer.json is commonly configured to start several development processes together, including:

- The Laravel development server.
- A queue worker.
- Laravel log monitoring through Pail.
- Vite, which serves frontend assets during development.

Install Spatie Laravel Permission
composer require spatie/laravel-permission

Once the command finishes, publish Spatie's configuration and migrations:
php artisan vendor:publish --provider="Spatie\Permission\PermissionServiceProvider"

php artisan migrate

Add Spatie's trait to the User model

app/Models/User.php use Spatie\Permission\Traits\HasRoles;
add HasRoles to the model's existing traits
use HasFactory, Notifiable, HasRoles;

It adds methods to the User model, including:
$user->assignRole('admin');

$user->hasRole('admin');

$user->hasPermissionTo('view employees');

$user->getRoleNames();

Role seeder + permisson seeder

<?php

namespace Database\Seeders;

use Illuminate\Database\Seeder;
use Spatie\Permission\Models\Role;
use Spatie\Permission\Models\Permission;
use Spatie\Permission\PermissionRegistrar;

class RolesAndPermissionsSeeder extends Seeder
{
    public function run(): void
    {
        // Clear cached permissions before defining them.
        app()[PermissionRegistrar::class]->forgetCachedPermissions();

        // Define the permissions available in the application.
        $permissions = [
            'view employees',
            'create employees',
            'edit employees',
            'delete employees',
        ];

        // Create each permission if it does not already exist.
        foreach ($permissions as $permission) {
            Permission::firstOrCreate([
                'name' => $permission,
                'guard_name' => 'web',
            ]);
        }

        // Admin can perform every employee operation.
        $admin = Role::firstOrCreate([
            'name' => 'admin',
            'guard_name' => 'web',
        ]);

        $admin->syncPermissions($permissions);

        // HR can view, create, and edit employees, but cannot delete.
        $hr = Role::firstOrCreate([
            'name' => 'hr',
            'guard_name' => 'web',
        ]);

        $hr->syncPermissions([
            'view employees',
            'create employees',
            'edit employees',
        ]);

        // Employee receives no general employee-management permissions.
        // Access to their own record will be handled later by a policy.
        Role::firstOrCreate([
            'name' => 'employee',
            'guard_name' => 'web',
        ]);

        // Clear the cached permission data after seeding.
        app()[PermissionRegistrar::class]->forgetCachedPermissions();
    }
}


